# Byte-exact files: never let git rewrite them on the way in or out.
#
# The vendored three.js bundles are documented as byte-identical copies, with their
# sha256 recorded in docs/VIEWER.md and embeddings/README.md. This machine has
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites line endings when a file is added -- that
# silently changes the blob (it turns CRLF into CRCRLF), so the recorded digest
# stops describing what is in the tree. `-text` turns the rewriting off for these
# paths; the golden `.npz` files are blocked from being committed at all by
# .gitignore, and this keeps a stray one from being mangled if that ever changes.
viewer/vendor/** -text
*.npz -text
